Package: hilldiv3
Title: Integral Analysis of Diversity Based on Hill Numbers
Version: 3.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Antton", "Alberdi", , "antton.alberdi@bio.ku.dk", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2875-6446"))
Description: Tools for analysing the diversity of biological communities
    (e.g. OTU/ASV/MAG tables) based on Hill numbers. 'hilldiv3' provides a
    unified framework for neutral, phylogenetic and functional diversity
    measurement, diversity partitioning, (dis)similarity measurement,
    diversity profiles, evenness and redundancy. The statistical framework
    encompasses richness, Shannon and Simpson diversity, Faith's PD,
    Rao's quadratic entropy and Sorensen/Unifrac-type dissimilarities, all
    grounded in a single Hill-number framework. Methods are described in
    Jost (2007) <doi:10.1890/06-1736.1>, Chao et al. (2010)
    <doi:10.1098/rstb.2010.0272>, Chiu et al. (2014) <doi:10.1890/12-0960.1>
    and reviewed in Alberdi & Gilbert (2019) <doi:10.1111/1755-0998.13014>.
